<article class="container pt-10 pb-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-9">
            <h1 class="pb-3">Network and edge</h1>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Routing the lab</h2>
            <p>
                A NanoPi R6S running FriendlyWrt is the router for the house and office networks.
                It handles DHCP and local DNS, so clients can find services by name and I can move a service without updating every client.
                Network policy lives at the router, where I can see which traffic crosses between networks or leaves for the internet.
            </p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Publishing the dev sites</h2>
            <p>
                Nginx Proxy Manager runs on the NanoPi and terminates public HTTPS for the CodeBuildDeploy dev sites.
                It forwards requests over WireGuard to a private Istio frontend on Azure Kubernetes Service, and it checks the upstream certificate using the hostname for each site.
                The public entry point is the reverse proxy.
                The AKS ingress is reached through the tunnel.
            </p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Maintaining the router</h2>
            <p>
                I keep a firmware recovery image and configuration backups.
                After a FriendlyWrt upgrade, I restored the network and service settings selectively so I could keep the new firmware and verify each part of the setup.
                I check routing and DNS from clients, then test HTTPS from outside the network to cover the full path.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</article>
